{"id":"92e4419a-ac8c-4ea4-bf47-2c7e35a13ede","recipient":"9d34f1cc-2595-4c4a-962f-f853c3e22d4e","sender":"209fa9e0-ee61-4880-99d5-289b12513ce8","priority":"MESSAGE_PRIORITY_HIGH","timestamp":"2026-09-24T19:02:58.969817200Z","renderDetails":{"messageTitle":"Message from UI Agent - QA/QC Data Health (browser)"},"content":"### Browser Agent UI-08 Report: Chrome Connection Failure\n\n**Status:** Unable to inspect `http://localhost:5173/qa-dashboard`. The connection to Chrome could not be established.\n\n**Error Details:**\n- `Could not connect to Chrome. Check if Chrome is running.`\n- `Cause: Could not find DevToolsActivePort for chrome at C:\\Users\\samsung\\AppData\\Local\\Google\\Chrome\\User Data\\DevToolsActivePort`\n\n**Troubleshooting Steps Required:**\n1. **Check DevToolsActivePort file:** Verify the `DevToolsActivePort` file in the Chrome user data directory (`C:\\Users\\samsung\\AppData\\Local\\Google\\Chrome\\User Data\\DevToolsActivePort`).\n2. **Enable Remote Debugging:** Ensure Google Chrome is running with remote debugging enabled, or navigate to `chrome://inspect/#remote-debugging` in Chrome and verify the appropriate remote target / debugging settings.\n3. **Check Port & Processes:** Check that the debugging port is open and verify whether multiple processes are listening on the port. If conflicting processes exist, terminate them before relaunching Chrome with remote debugging.\n\nOnce Chrome is running with remote debugging active, re-run this agent to perform the QA dashboard inspection.\n\n*(Note: The recording of this session is available in the conversation artifacts.)*","sourceMetadata":{"tool":{"conversationId":"209fa9e0-ee61-4880-99d5-289b12513ce8","stepIndex":6,"toolCall":{"id":"call_653490","name":"send_message","argumentsJson":"{\"Message\":\"### Browser Agent UI-08 Report: Chrome Connection Failure\\n\\n**Status:** Unable to inspect `http://localhost:5173/qa-dashboard`. The connection to Chrome could not be established.\\n\\n**Error Details:**\\n- `Could not connect to Chrome. Check if Chrome is running.`\\n- `Cause: Could not find DevToolsActivePort for chrome at C:\\\\Users\\\\samsung\\\\AppData\\\\Local\\\\Google\\\\Chrome\\\\User Data\\\\DevToolsActivePort`\\n\\n**Troubleshooting Steps Required:**\\n1. **Check DevToolsActivePort file:** Verify the `DevToolsActivePort` file in the Chrome user data directory (`C:\\\\Users\\\\samsung\\\\AppData\\\\Local\\\\Google\\\\Chrome\\\\User Data\\\\DevToolsActivePort`).\\n2. **Enable Remote Debugging:** Ensure Google Chrome is running with remote debugging enabled, or navigate to `chrome://inspect/#remote-debugging` in Chrome and verify the appropriate remote target / debugging settings.\\n3. **Check Port \\u0026 Processes:** Check that the debugging port is open and verify whether multiple processes are listening on the port. If conflicting processes exist, terminate them before relaunching Chrome with remote debugging.\\n\\nOnce Chrome is running with remote debugging active, re-run this agent to perform the QA dashboard inspection.\\n\\n*(Note: The recording of this session is available in the conversation artifacts.)*\",\"Recipient\":\"9d34f1cc-2595-4c4a-962f-f853c3e22d4e\",\"toolAction\":\"Sending Chrome connection failure report to parent agent\",\"toolSummary\":\"Send failure report to parent\"}","thinkingSignature":""}}}}